@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy Policy";
}

<div class="container py-5">
    <div class="max-w-800 mx-auto cc-surface-card p-5">
        <h1 class="h2 fw-bold mb-3">Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="text-muted small mb-4">Last Updated: October 2026</p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">1. Data Minimization & Security</h5>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            CardCompass respects your privacy. We <strong>never</strong> request, store, or process full credit card numbers, CVV codes, ATM PINs, net banking passwords, or Aadhaar numbers.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">2. Recommendation Tool Inputs</h5>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            Spending figures entered into our Recommendation Wizard and Rewards Calculator can be used anonymously without an account. When entered by an authenticated user, data is securely stored and isolated in your private user profile for your convenience.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">3. User Isolation & Authentication</h5>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            User accounts are protected by ASP.NET Core Identity with hashed credentials, anti-forgery tokens, and strict server-side authorization filters. No user can access or view another user's saved cards, expenses, or comparisons.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mt-4">4. Cookies & Session Storage</h5>
        <p class="text-muted small">
            CardCompass uses essential authentication cookies and local storage only for comparison tray management and user login sessions. We do not sell your personal data to third-party telemarketers or loan agents.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
